From 66312e087d71a378b0190dbddc374f76c2c64527 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: f <f@f>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 21:53:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: iris: free the controls of an instance whose open() is
 refused

iris_vdec_inst_init() has set the control handler up by the time
iris_add_session() refuses the instance; the path that frees the two
formats leaves the handler's own allocations behind. iris_close() frees
it; do the same here.

Local, not upstream. It follows the upstream patch that refuses open()
at the session limit and shares its failure path.
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vidc.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vidc.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vidc.c
index 6997593839..1c758e64cf 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vidc.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vidc.c
@@ -214,6 +214,7 @@ int iris_open(struct file *filp)
 	return 0;
 
 fail_inst_deinit:
+	v4l2_ctrl_handler_free(&inst->ctrl_handler);
 	kfree(inst->fmt_src);
 	kfree(inst->fmt_dst);
 fail_m2m_ctx_release:
